{title: Rise Up, O Men of God}
{artist: William P. Merrill / William H. Walter}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Closing}
{key: A}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 110}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (United Methodist Hymnal (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1989), # 576)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[E]Rise [A]up, O [C#]men [A]of [D]God!
[A]Have [D]done [A]with [B7]lesser [E]things.
[E]Give [A]heart and [D]mind and [Bm]soul and [E]strength
[E]To [D]serve the [E7]King of [A]kings.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[E]Rise [A]up, O [C#]men [A]of [D]God!
[A]The [D]king[A]dom [B7]tarries [E]long.
[E]Bring [A]in the [D]day of [Bm]brother[E]hood
[E]And [D]end the [E7]night of [A]wrong.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[E]Rise [A]up, O [C#]men [A]of [D]God!
[A]The [D]church [A]for [B7]you doth [E]wait,
[E]Her [A]strength un[D]equal [Bm]to her [E]task;
[E]Rise [D]up and [E7]make her [A]great!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[E]Lift [A]high the [C#]cross [A]of [D]Christ!
[A]Tread [D]where [A]His [B7]feet have [E]trod.
[E]As [A]brothers [D]of the [Bm]Son of [E]Man,
[E]Rise [D]up, O [E7]men of [A]God!
{end_of_verse}
